<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Western Deep output unaffected by accident.</title>
<headline>Western Deep output unaffected by accident.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>An accident at Western Deep Levels east mine on Monday will have no material impact on production since only one production panel was affected, managers Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd said on Tuesday in response to investor queries.</p>
<p>One mineworker was killed and several injured in the accident caused by a seismic event which measured 3.1 on the Richter scale.</p>
<p>Western Deep produced 7,830 kg of gold in the three months to end September.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
